            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air Leakage Areas:



Front window seal is not working properly allowing air leakage. May need to replace.



Right hinged window is very leaky.



Front bedroom window 



Utilidor area is very leaky and should be assessed



Gas supply entry into the crawlspace.



Back door needs new weather stripping.



Left Bedroom window is broke and needs to be replaced.



Attic Hatch is very leaky, could install a gasket/seal around edges of the hatch



Ceiling fixtures showing leakage.



</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>Add approximately R-15 of insulation on the exterior of the building.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on insulation upgrades and the criteria for these products.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>Add approximately R-30 attic insulation to the flat portion of the ceiling. Some of the batt insulation is not properly installed so that should be assessed before performing any upgrades. 



There are air leaks around the ceiling fixtures as well. These should be properly sealed before installing additional insulation.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on insulation upgrades and the criteria for these products.</ceilings>
                <ceilingsCathedral>Sloped Ceiling area should be filled with spray foam, Exisiting insulation can be fully removed and have each cavity filled with spray foam. This will maximize the insulation value for the limited space available.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on insulation upgrades and the criteria for these products.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <windows>Left bedroom window is broke and does not close all the way. This should be priority for replacing.



Upgrade windows to energy star zone 3 rated.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on windows/doors and the criteria for these products.</windows>
                <VentilationSystem>Bathroom Fan is not working properly and should be replaced. Damper may have failed. 



If there are air sealing upgrades completed to the home, it will make it tighter, but it will not allow for the home to breathe as it was before. A mechanical ventilation system such as an HRV/ERV should be installed to allow the home to be properly ventilated. Not installing a system after air sealing can lead to issues with mold and mildew.



The HRV/ERV will recover heated exhaust air via a heat exchanger and preheat supply air with the extracted heat, making the units very efficient. 



HRV = Heat Recovery Ventilator

ERV = Enthalpy Recovery Ventilator



ERV also can control indoor humidity levels as well.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on ventilation systems and the criteria for these products.

</VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>Upgrade furnace to a condensing gas boiler with a 95% AFUE. 



Install a digital or smart thermostat to help reduce fuell consumption.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on heating system upgrades and the criteria for these products.</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
